media: qcom: camss: OPE: bound the stride and re-check param block sizes

Two checks on what userspace hands the OPE:

- A bytesperline larger than needed was taken as is, so a huge value
  made bytesperline * height overflow the 32-bit sizeimage, and the
  buffers could be smaller than what the engines fetch and write.
  Bound it to 4 bytes per pixel of the widest frame.

- The params buffer is parsed while it is still mapped to userspace,
  after v4l2_isp_params_validate_buffer() checked it. The parse loop
  re-checked each block size against what is left, but not against the
  size of its type, so a block shrunk in between let the handler copy
  past it. Check that too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/core.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/core.c
index 0345ba25d..1775555dd 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/core.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/core.c
@@ -1912,8 +1912,9 @@ static const struct ope_fmt *ope_fmt_try(struct ope_dev *ope, bool is_output,
 	else
 		bytesperline = pix->width * fmt->depth / 8;
 
+	/* a larger stride from userspace is kept, bounded so sizeimage cannot overflow */
 	if (pix->plane_fmt[0].bytesperline > bytesperline)
-		bytesperline = pix->plane_fmt[0].bytesperline;
+		bytesperline = min_t(u32, pix->plane_fmt[0].bytesperline, OPE_MAX_W * 4);
 
 	/*
 	 * The WE requires the C plane base address to be 16-byte aligned.
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/params.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/params.c
index ffdabf93a..0eddac876 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/params.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/ope/params.c
@@ -60,6 +60,12 @@ int camss_isp_params_apply(struct device *dev,
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
 
+		/* re-checked: the buffer is shared with userspace and may have changed */
+		if (type < num_handlers && handlers[type] && bsize < type_info[type].size) {
+			dev_dbg(dev, "params: block type %u too small (%u)\n", type, bsize);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+
 		if (type < num_handlers && handlers[type])
 			handlers[type](priv, block);
 		else
